{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom","id":1388991,"title":"Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-16T11:06:13-07:00","id":1388991,"title":"Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom","content":"I really liked this book. The Laibon Legacies are both interesting and different than regular Western Kindred. My personal opinion is that the Laibon are not really Cainites, but there\u2019s enough evidence to go either way. This book may not be that useful unless you\u2019re running or playing in a Vampire game set in Africa, but it\u2019s defo interesting to read.<br /> <br /> There. Not bad for being a little buzzed \ud83d\ude02.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:18:58-07:00","id":1389104,"title":"","content":"Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary also contains some updated info about the Laibon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:37:27-07:00","id":1389111,"title":"","content":"I think the Beckett's Jyhad Diary entry was basically, &quot;Yes, we're probably the same species but you're descended from US not the other way around if we're at all logical about this. Oh and it's probable that we're older than the Caine myth.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:53:30-07:00","id":1389118,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea of African vampires being a different species from Cainites is odd, because Caine is a middle-eastern myth, and the &quot;middle-east&quot; is essentially eastern Africa and western Asia. If &quot;western&quot; vampires had come first, one would think that something like the first vampire being Odin would be predominate. Cainites' own mythology implies an immigration from either Africa or western Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:57:00-07:00","id":1389119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389118#post1389118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the idea of African vampires being a different species from Cainites is odd, because Caine is a middle-eastern myth, and the &quot;middle-east&quot; is essentially eastern Africa and western Asia. If &quot;western&quot; vampires had come first, one would think that something like the first vampire being Odin would be predominate. Cainites' own mythology implies an immigration from either Africa or western Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the BJD chapters would be a good basis for the update of the Wan Kuei because it was nicely cosmopolitan. Some were Christian, others African animist, others a little of both, some Muslim, and so on.<br /> <br /> More representative of Africa as a whole and its diversity of myths as well as peoples.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T17:10:53-07:00","id":1389122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389119#post1389119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the BJD chapters would be a good basis for the update of the Wan Kuei because it was nicely cosmopolitan. Some were Christian, others African animist, others a little of both, some Muslim, and so on.<br /> <br /> More representative of Africa as a whole and its diversity of myths as well as peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn\u2019t that pretty much what we got. In the Ebony Kingdom book it\u2019s also seeded with the idea they are the oldest vampire territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T17:21:48-07:00","id":1389124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389122#post1389122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn\u2019t that pretty much what we got. In the Ebony Kingdom book it\u2019s also seeded with the idea they are the oldest vampire territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> I was saying they should be handled like the Laibon were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:47:31-07:00","id":1389152,"title":"","content":"A few of the Liabon are also discussed in the V20 Dark Ages book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25885-ozymandias242","name":"Ozymandias242","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T21:47:48-07:00","id":1389190,"title":"","content":"In order for Western Cainites to be descended from the Laibon, Eden would have to be somewhere in Africa. Which I guess is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:22:50-07:00","id":1389196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389190#post1389190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for Western Cainites to be descended from the Laibon, Eden would have to be somewhere in Africa. Which I guess is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there's nothing especially necessary about putting Enoch or the other mythical locations of Noddism in the Middle East versus Africa itself.<br /> <br /> Really, I think the only indications it was in the ME is the fact that the Gehenna Crusade has stumbled upon a shit ton of old ass vampires there.<br /> <br /> Even then, the Gehenna Crusade is apparently also taking place in North Africa. Mind you, that just may be the Sabbat going to Tunsia and getting their ass handed to them by Troile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T23:08:28-07:00","id":1389205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389196#post1389196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, the Gehenna Crusade is apparently also taking place in North Africa. Mind you, that just may be the Sabbat going to Tunsia and getting their ass handed to them by Troile.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my new headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T03:56:30-07:00","id":1389237,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:04:50-07:00","id":1389284,"title":"","content":"We have a confirmed Mitochondrial Eve from whom we all descend so it stands to reason that there was, at some point, a first vampire from whom all others descend and whoever it was they may as well be called Caine.<br /> <br /> Even if they were not the literal child of Mitochondrial Eve, they would still be a direct descendant of her and since this vampire\u2019s actual name is lost to history (Cain\u2019s name in the Bible means either \u201csmith/builder\u201d; likely in reference to building Enoch; or \u201cto get/begotten\u201d in the same way that Adam is \u201cMan\u201d and Eve is \u201clife-giver\u201d) Caine is as good term for this first vampire as any.<br /> <br /> Both Mitochondrial Eve and Y-chromosome Adam existed c. 150k years ago and the earliest evidence of the humans from which we\u2019re all descended leaving Africa is c. 125k years ago (into the Middle East... a region one could say is \u201cEast of Eden.\u201d<br /> <br /> Presuming that \u201cCaine\u201d came into being somewhere in that time range it\u2019s entirely possible for \u201chim\u201d (there\u2019s probably a 50/50 chance whoever the first vampire was was actually a woman) it\u2019s sensible to believe that both Laibon and Western Kindred share a common ancestor. This common ancestor, by definition, would also have preceded the first Wan Kuei by millennia since no modern humans had yet reached the Middle Kingdom (so if you wanted to do a \u201cClan Wan Kuei\u201d instead of the KotE \u201cRisen\u201d you could certainly justify it in the setting).<br /> <br /> Another really wild thought to consider is that \u201cBlood Caine\u201d (in the vein of MitoEve) and \u201cWestern Caine\u201d (the one Western Kindred count their generations from) don\u2019t have to be the same person.<br /> <br /> There could be a hypothetical Generation 0 (of which Lilith might have been a member) or even a Generation -169 (13x13) prior to the Caine that Western Kindred count their generations from.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, just as Tremere and Giovanni and Troile ate their way up to Antediluvian status, maybe Western Caine ate his way up to 1st Generation; diablerizing whoever had that power at the time (because that\u2019s something that could have happened dozens of times over a span of 150k years).<br /> <br /> Maybe Gehenna is just a sort of contest of champions\u201d where younger vampires get eaten as fuel for the ancients to kill each other off until one of them diablerizes the current 1st Generation to become a \u201cNew Caine\u201d who sire progeny and starts the process all over again. Thin-bloods ot 14+ generation may have occurred multiple times before recorded history... there\u2019s just little evidence of them because after 15k years any of the few who did survive that Gehenna either died later, diablerized their way up to a lower generation and/or just went into torpor and never woke back up (and are thus completely unaware of scientific advances like agriculture, the wheel and written language).<br /> <br /> Lilith and The Crone might have been some of the last survivors of the previous cycle (Lilith being one who won the last round, a Gen 0 essentially, who Embraced Caine... while the Crone was a higher generation survivor of the last round who tricked him into a blood bond).<br /> <br /> That could also explain certain confusions regarding who\u2019s what generation and who sired who among the eldest generations... because diablerie has always gone on and thus some of the Clan founders might be 2nd Gen now or they replaced a prior 3rd Gen before written language even existed to record it.<br /> <br /> Hell, given what \u201cLife After People\u201d depicted, modern civilizations could have risen and fallen so hard that nothing remains half-a-dozen times in the span between MitoEve and now. Maybe those pale \u201cancient aliens\u201d who taught the Egyptians to build the pyramids were actually the last vampires of the previous cycle.<br /> <br /> You can go as crazy as you want to get with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:26:48-07:00","id":1389292,"title":"","content":"Idk exactly what Mitochondrial means<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think about the Crone being the founder of the Lhiannan bloodline? She began as Second Gen but dropped down to Third when she Embraced a childe because of the Lhiannan flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:30:58-07:00","id":1389295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389237#post1389237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02</div> </div> </div> </div>What's extra funny is I'm seeing the Sabbat digging up all of the Carthagian vampires they salted the Earth to contain, only to get eaten by them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389292#post1389292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idk exactly what Mitochondrial means<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think about the Crone being the founder of the Lhiannan bloodline? She began as Second Gen but dropped down to Third when she Embraced a childe because of the Lhiannan flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, there's this 14 year old girl's remains in Africa that literally all of humanity is descended from.<br /> <br /> We know because we did a DNA test and we all have a bit of her in us.<br /> <br /> Hence mitcochondria (which George Lucas named the midiclorians after) and Eve.<br /> <br /> It was used in Battlestar Galactica as a plot point (and really sucks for the character). She is useful for the context of Noddism in the fact that, yes, Africa is the birthplace of all of humanity and if you want to suggest that there ever was a historical Nod then that's where you should put it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-17-2020, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:27:20-07:00","id":1389322,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I knew it had something to do with cell structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:25:27-07:00","id":1389336,"title":"","content":"To further elaborate, Mitochondria are a part of your DNA that are transmitted from mother to child in an unbroken line and one of the main ways that geneticists track population groups through history.<br /> <br /> Also, just to clarify, they don\u2019t actually have a specific set of remains that is the Mitochondrial Eve... but because Mitochondrial DNA changes at a consistent rate they\u2019re able calculate roughly when this individual existed (150k is just a median range... estimates are she lived 100-200k years ago).<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is that Adam, Eve and many other early Biblical names are better understood as titles (Man, Life-Giver) than actual given names. So regardless of who they actually were, there was a First Vampire from whom all others descend and that First Vampire may as well have the title Caine because their actual name is lost to history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:29:19-07:00","id":1389340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.livescience.com/mitochondrial-eve-first-human-homeland.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/4yZjPpvRyhWm4WE2A9RvdZ-2000-80.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.livescience.com/mitochondrial-eve-first-human-homeland.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Scientists Think They've Found 'Mitochondrial Eve's' First Homeland </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.livescience.com/mitochondrial-eve-first-human-homeland.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.livescience.com/mitochondrial-eve-first-human-homeland.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Today it's a desert. Two hundred thousand years ago, perhaps it was home. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's arguably the &quot;historical&quot; Eden for a WOD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:37:30-07:00","id":1389419,"title":"","content":"I tend to see it as all as originating from a curse. It could be the same curse that changed in various ways, or it could be different curses. Or the same curse with different (possibly related) progenitors. Or different curses with different progenitors. There's alot of mutability even when you confine it to just 'Cainite' curses that you could probably find some workaround.. the only question is if you really need/want one aspect to dominate over others. <br /> <br /> I mean Caine was a farmer who was cursed. Perhaps the Laibon descend from a progenitor (who knew or was related to Caine) who was also cursed, and then the Wan Kuei descend from a different progenitor cursed in yet a different way (probably something with warrior origins.) <br /> <br /> Given the way MtA's Fractured Cosmos (and the DtF equivalent) worked out, you can technically have a Kenobi-style 'certain point of view' style 'truth'. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T16:23:05-07:00","id":1389486,"title":"","content":"I don't have the resources to go into details fully here but the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom book is rather explicit about the Laibon being descended from a figure who while similar to is distinct from Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T16:56:20-07:00","id":1389491,"title":"","content":"Why all the speculation, just read the book. As I remember (it was a long time ago), The origin story of the Laibon is pretty close to that of original kindreds. The progenitor of them is called Cagn (!), they have generations and the Legacies are identifiable as Clans or Bloodlines from Clans, some have even the same names (followers of Set for example). There is no doubt that the Laibon are just the same kind of creature as the Kindreds are, they have just a different relationship to spirituality. We know, that believe systems change how things are in the WoD, and therefore the Laibon Legacies have this weird (cool) thing with having two paths (of enlightenment). Since Dark Ages established (and later on every Vampire Book that talked about it) that a paths/roads provide an aura, that changes how the Vampire in question is perceived by other individuals, it is even mechanically pretty close in line with how kindreds are.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately did V20 Dark Ages KotEK a big disservice by creating \u201cnew\u201d Legecies that just not fit in logically (historical accurate, maybe, great as Requiem bloodlines, unfortunately nonsensical for Dark Ages and VtM in general).<br /> <br /> I think, if the KotEK ever show up again in V5 They will be handled as Bloodlines (changed Discipline and a unique Loresheet) of the usual clans. And I think they will end up with a special Touchstone option, that represents either if they are more drown to the physical or spiritual world or if they are in balance. But I think we will see paths of enlightenment and maybe even the Kindreds of the east before, thins the KotEK never got much attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T17:02:44-07:00","id":1389494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389486#post1389486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the resources to go into details fully here but the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom book is rather explicit about the Laibon being descended from a figure who while similar to is distinct from Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have fun with the Caine origin in my games. I've had the following as stories Kindred have claimed:<br /> <br /> * Vampires are descended from Romulus and Remus (another fratricide story)<br /> * Vampires are descended from Baldur after Loki's trickery made him come back &quot;wrong.&quot;<br /> * Vampires are descended from Set and Osiris because OBVIOUSLY, their fratricide predates Cain.<br /> * Vampires are the children of Hecate, who taught the Thirteen magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:10:01-07:00","id":1389509,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> I read the Cagn origin story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T19:17:09-07:00","id":1389527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389119#post1389119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the BJD chapters would be a good basis for the update of the Wan Kuei because it was nicely cosmopolitan. Some were Christian, others African animist, others a little of both, some Muslim, and so on.<br /> <br /> More representative of Africa as a whole and its diversity of myths as well as peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much agreed. It\u2019s also a great chapter in the way it suggests the Laibon and Kindred could be the same species yet operate differently in some rather basic ways. Like how Generation and Gehenna might be a self-imposed limitation of certain lineages, not how vampires have to be. Or how they were originally. Maybe the Antediluvians\u2019 great sin was beginning this whole cycle in the first place, since they could have chosen to power down and <i>not</i> become all-consuming horrors.<br /> <br /> The Wan Gui could be a similarly ancient culture of vampires who never developed the Caine myth or suffer from inevitable generational thinning or the fear of Lovecraftian ancestors. But of course they\u2019d have their own problems because we don\u2019t want to go down the \u201cenlightened orientals\u201d road again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T19:31:16-07:00","id":1389532,"title":"","content":"The Kuei-Jin don't have a Caine myth or generational thinning because they don't have embraces. Every Kuei-Jin is an escaped soul from the Thousand Hells that has cleaved, sneaked, or silver-tongued itself from that realm back into their bodies. They have nothing to do with Caine or Gehenna, mostly their own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T21:17:26-07:00","id":1389557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389532#post1389532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kuei-Jin don't have a Caine myth or generational thinning because they don't have embraces. Every Kuei-Jin is an escaped soul from the Thousand Hells that has cleaved, sneaked, or silver-tongued itself from that realm back into their bodies. They have nothing to do with Caine or Gehenna, mostly their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I\u2019m reimagining them instead as something more akin to the Laibon. I\u2019ve never been comfortable with \u201cour vampires are totally different because Asian.\u201d I think Kindred should be Kindred, but that some of our assumptions about the Kindred might not be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T00:34:35-07:00","id":1389584,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> very good point. I Liked your post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T01:09:15-07:00","id":1389589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389557#post1389557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know. I\u2019m reimagining them instead as something more akin to the Laibon. I\u2019ve never been comfortable with \u201cour vampires are totally different because Asian.\u201d I think Kindred should be Kindred, but that some of our assumptions about the Kindred might not be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your post a lot; however, I think &quot;vampires should be vampires&quot;, but maybe not all vampires are &quot;Kindred&quot;. And maybe all of them descend from... the same ancestors? Caine? Ur-wampyr? But not all of them know about it, or agree...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T03:11:53-07:00","id":1389607,"title":"","content":"My personal headcanon about vampire... \u201cevolution\u201d goes like this:<br /> <br /> Wan Gui (or how you want to call Asian vampires) are basically a very special case of Risen, who managed to sustain their existence by stealing blood/chi from the living.<br /> <br /> Cain (Maine even not one person but several individuals in the same region with a shared story) was basically a Wan Gui, risen because his brother was killed, unable to find revenge, because he was the murder him self.<br /> <br /> Due to a lack of knowledge, since he was alone, he remained on the yin side of existence and didn\u2019t learn to get chi without drinking blood.<br /> <br /> Due to the teachings of Lilith and the Cron (the first either a celestial being or a Wan Gui her self, the second probably a hedge mage) he learned some rituals he can die with Vampiric blood. Create children, blood bond other beings and so on.<br /> I think this rituals could be learned by Wan Gui too, just like some kindred, as Saulot (and he was not the only one) learned Wan Gui techniques. It is just the mindset and the culture of both kinds of vampires, that makes it very unlikely to understand how close both groups actually are.<br /> <br /> Now let\u2019s talk about Laibon. They Are basically kindred that went to Africa, where they found much les cities and developed a more solitary lifestyle than there western and eastern relatives. In insulation it was much easier to develop several bloodlines due to a lack of organization. And they had the opportunity to rediscover some of the spiritual aspects of the Wan Gui. The Human/Beast duality, for example.<br /> <br /> Now we have the drowned legacies. I think they are similar to the Laibon, basically Kindred, but with a unique worldview. Or, maybe, they are the children of forgotten antediluvians or even another \u201cVampire Patient Zero\u201d, who ones was similar to a Wan Gui, just like Cain, but had to learn the rules on his own.<br /> <br /> Long story short: it is all the same but different!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T03:31:52-07:00","id":1389615,"title":"","content":"Archaeology wise:<br /> <br /> * Caine was born in Africa. Enoch was in North Africa, probably near Carthage for maximum irony.<br /> * Caine was cursed by God and rose from the dead after he died of whatever actually killed him.<br /> * The Laibon are descendants of the &quot;original&quot; Kindred that were the 4th generation sired by the Third while Enoch was the capital of vampiredom.<br /> * After the Flood, Ventrue went to the Middle East with other 13 and set up their own Second City. So the European vampires are descendants of the Second City not the First City.<br /> * The obnoxiousness of the modern vampires are due to being descended from Ventrue's laws.<br /> * Set actually said &quot;Screw this&quot; first and stayed in Egypt, separate from the Ventrue's reign. Osiris is possibly one of Ventrue's childer.<br /> * Haqim and Ventrue feuded for control over the rulership of Kindred. Saulot Embraced the Baali and they became an enemy to the Middle Eastern Kindred.<br /> * Tzimisce eventually left for Eastern Europe. Ravnos for India. Saulot for China.<br /> * Troile killed Brujah and fought a revolt that she lost, causing the Second City to be destroyed.<br /> * The surviving vampires went to the rest of the Middle East and other locations.<br /> * Saulot experimented with supernatural magic and may have made contact with the Yama Kings, screwing up the entirety of the Heavens and Hells. The Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei are a product of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-18-2020, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:00:42-07:00","id":1389622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389615#post1389615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archaeology wise:<br /> <br /> * Caine was born in Africa. Enoch was in North Africa, probably near Carthage for maximum irony.<br /> * Caine was cursed by God and rose from the dead after he died of whatever actually killed him.<br /> * The Laibon are descendants of the &quot;original&quot; Kindred that were the 4th generation sired by the Third while Enoch was the capital of vampiredom.<br /> * After the Flood, Ventrue went to the Middle East with other 13 and set up their own Second City. So the European vampires are descendants of the Second City not the First City.<br /> * The obnoxiousness of the modern vampires are due to being descended from Ventrue's laws.<br /> * Set actually said &quot;Screw this&quot; first and stayed in Egypt, separate from the Ventrue.<br /> * Haqim and Ventrue feuded for control over the rulership of Kindred. Saulot Embraced the Baali and they became an enemy to the Middle Eastern Kindred.<br /> * Tzimisce eventually left for Eastern Europe. Ravnos for India. Saulot for China.<br /> * Troile killed Brujah and fought a revolt that she lost, causing the Second City to be destroyed.<br /> * The surviving vampires went to the rest of the Middle East and other locations.<br /> * Saulot experimented with supernatural magic and may have made contact with the Yama Kings, screwing up the entirety of the Heavens and Hells. The Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei are a product of this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty cool summary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:09:11-07:00","id":1389624,"title":"","content":"Bah, it's almost entirely own invention but it could be something that Beckett believes.<br /> <br /> He'd get annoyed if someone said, &quot;No, no, you didn't include the Demon War and flying cities! Or the Scarlet Empress!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;SHUT UP, ANATOLE! EVOLUTION IS REAL!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:43:12-07:00","id":1389630,"title":"","content":"I always thought Osiris was a Ventrue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:57:59-07:00","id":1389633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389615#post1389615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archaeology wise:<br /> <br /> * Caine was born in Africa. Enoch was in North Africa, probably near Carthage for maximum irony.<br /> * Caine was cursed by God and rose from the dead after he died of whatever actually killed him.<br /> * The Laibon are descendants of the &amp;quot;original&amp;quot; Kindred that were the 4th generation sired by the Third while Enoch was the capital of vampiredom.<br /> * After the Flood, Ventrue went to the Middle East with other 13 and set up their own Second City. So the European vampires are descendants of the Second City not the First City.<br /> * The obnoxiousness of the modern vampires are due to being descended from Ventrue's laws.<br /> * Set actually said &amp;quot;Screw this&amp;quot; first and stayed in Egypt, separate from the Ventrue's reign. Osiris is possibly one of Ventrue's childer.<br /> * Haqim and Ventrue feuded for control over the rulership of Kindred. Saulot Embraced the Baali and they became an enemy to the Middle Eastern Kindred.<br /> * Tzimisce eventually left for Eastern Europe. Ravnos for India. Saulot for China.<br /> * Troile killed Brujah and fought a revolt that she lost, causing the Second City to be destroyed.<br /> * The surviving vampires went to the rest of the Middle East and other locations.<br /> * Saulot experimented with supernatural magic and may have made contact with the Yama Kings, screwing up the entirety of the Heavens and Hells. The Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei are a product of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes a lot of sense and fits with my version too, beside from the last assumption. I think old Asian vampires would strongly disagree, if you claim that they are created by Saulot. It is him they call a traitor and it is Saulot who learned their secrets, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:05:39-07:00","id":1389637,"title":"","content":"I know, that was very Cainite centric. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:59:55-07:00","id":1389669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389589#post1389589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your post a lot; however, I think &quot;vampires should be vampires&quot;, but maybe not all vampires are &quot;Kindred&quot;. And maybe all of them descend from... the same ancestors? Caine? Ur-wampyr? But not all of them know about it, or agree...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we agree. I was using \u201cKindred\u201d to mean \u201csame species\u201d rather than \u201csame culture.\u201d I think these vampires can have widely differing concepts of their own origins without actually being different types of creature. <br /> <br /> Also, multiple separate vampire origins is kind of Requiem\u2019s thing. And that\u2019s without getting into the terrible orientalism and cultural essentialism of KotE, which has not aged well at all. KotEK, by contrast, has aged much better, as it seems to understand that Africa and Eurasia have always been connected, even if Europeans have often failed to understand Africa on its own terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:39:55-07:00","id":1389730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389124#post1389124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> I was saying they should be handled like the Laibon were.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh please no, let them be something different and new (But then I didn't like the way Ebony kingdom was 'oh yea your myths are totally false, vampires are a result of Yhwh's curse, get over it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:04:54-07:00","id":1389802,"title":"","content":"Yes, there should be completely different and unrelated vampires that only appear in areas with high concentrations of East Asian people, because Asians and their ancient mystical ways are essentially different from other... oh no, wait, it\u2019s the 21st century, and that\u2019s gross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:20:46-07:00","id":1389806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389802#post1389802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there should be completely different and unrelated vampires that only appear in areas with high concentrations of East Asian people, because Asians and their ancient mystical ways are essentially different from other... oh no, wait, it\u2019s the 21st century, and that\u2019s gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it\u2019s not just East Asian, they are tied to areas ranging from India to Japan to Siberia and The nomads of the steps.<br /> <br /> Funny how it\u2019s not gross to ham fist them into Abrahamic origins. Meanwhile when they experimented with designing the Middle Kingdom they fit with all the splats in their setting, perfectly crossover friendly, it\u2019s almost like it was intentionally an experiment in building a cohesive setting.<br /> <br /> But your right it would have been better to just have them ruled over by Europeans of the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:41:05-07:00","id":1389812,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a vast excluded middle between making them a special Asian species, that arises because of special magical Asian beliefs, and making them subjects of the Camarilla. Neither the Laibon nor the Ashirra are under the Camarilla. A sect is just a sect, not a species. Nor does Abraham have anything to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:14:13-07:00","id":1389822,"title":"","content":"Abrahamic notions DO have alot involved. The Kuei-Jin have a very interesting cosmology and reasoning to be the way they are essentially that involves the August Personage of Jade. No where in the origins of the Kuei-Jin is Caine involved- they explicitly came about with the 10,000 immortals. They have no generation, the way their inner &quot;Beast&quot; acts is more akin to a Wraith's shadow, different outlook, etc. Its more than &quot;special magical Asian beliefs&quot;.. The most silly thing about the whole Caine and Abrahamic god thing is how the WW writers only make THAT real/legitimate when before Abrahamic beliefs were even thought of in our reality (which oWoD mirrors) that were tons of different faiths (Greek pantheons, Egypt pantheons, various sub-saharan religions, Germanic, and a shit ton more).<br /> <br /> EDIT: And honestly this problem regarding VTM would've never been a problem if WW never dabled in Abrahamic religion to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:25:32-07:00","id":1389824,"title":"","content":"The idea that the Noddist Caine myth is literally and objectively true is something you hear on the internet. It\u2019s something the actual published books have been inviting us to question since the beginning. Even a substantial portion of the vampires in the setting don\u2019t believe it. Yes, even most of the Noddist scholars, barring the Sabbat. The Kindred have a number of competing origin myths.<br /> <br /> The existence of Generation as a phenomenon by itself doesn\u2019t prove the myth true. Nor does the existence of the \u201cAntediluvians\u201d (just as their name doesn\u2019t itself prove that there was a great flood). There could be any number of explanations for these phenomena (the Laibon have one theory).<br /> <br /> The Caine myth makes sense in the setting since in Europe and America the two main sects came out of medieval Europe, so of course they saw the world through a Christianizing lens. It would be odd if they didn\u2019t. I\u2019d also expect East Asia to have a quasi-Buddhist lens for interpreting their existence. The concept of a sect that represents that is sound. The actual execution in KotE is not. It takes something that should be cultural and turns it into something that falls into countless orientalist fallacies and pitfalls. Context is a thing. The essential difference between East and West is one of those fallacies, incidentally. There\u2019s no working around that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-18-2020, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:31:17-07:00","id":1389825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389822#post1389822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abrahamic notions DO have alot involved. The Kuei-Jin have a very interesting cosmology and reasoning to be the way they are essentially that involves the August Personage of Jade. No where in the origins of the Kuei-Jin is Caine involved- they explicitly came about with the 10,000 immortals. They have no generation, the way their inner &quot;Beast&quot; acts is more akin to a Wraith's shadow, different outlook, etc. Its more than &quot;special magical Asian beliefs&quot;.. <b>The most silly thing about the whole Caine and Abrahamic god thing is how the WW writers only make THAT real/legitimate when before Abrahamic beliefs were even thought of in our reality (which oWoD mirrors) that were tons of different faiths (Greek pantheons, Egypt pantheons, various sub-saharan religions, Germanic, and a shit ton more).</b><br /> <br /> EDIT: And honestly this problem regarding VTM would've never been a problem if WW never dabled in Abrahamic religion to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to explain what the problem with that logic is.<br /> <br /> So which of these contradictory religions is the correct one?<br /> <br /> The premise of V:TM is that a certain element of cultural mythology is correct: in this case, vampires. However, a simple fact of plenty of mythologies is that they are mutually contradictory. If you make Set an actual god then Judaism is incorrect. If you make Hinduism correct then everything else is incorrect. Some groups like DC Comics and Vertigo make all religious mutually true (and thus, ironically, mutually incorrect) but in this case they chose to tie the myth of the vampire to Christianity because it's a Christian myth. Just like they tied werewolves to nature-worshiping animism and explitly make Christianity wrong in that gameline.<br /> <br /> You can make an argument that vampires should be divorced from religious context completely but that is a VERY different game than Vampire as it is easily the most religious and mystical interpretation of vampires in all of undead fiction.<br /> <br /> (Also, FYI, Abrahamic religion is 4000 years old, so it's not actually remotely a &quot;new&quot; religion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-18-2020, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:44:59-07:00","id":1389830,"title":"","content":"And I would say there\u2019s no such thing as Abrahamic religion as a single phenomenon. And while it has bronze-age origins, it probably didn\u2019t coalesce into its familiar monotheistic character until around the Chaldean period. But that\u2019s not really the point.<br /> <br /> The point is that, while the familiar Noddism has clearly been filtered through a Christian lens because of its recent reception, it\u2019s not actually the same thing as Christianity, or even very compatible with it.<br /> <br /> But none of that ultimately matters, given that within the setting Noddism is a dominant cultural narrative, not the objective reality. I mean, hell, Beckett, the most iconic Noddist scholar of the whole line, believes it consists of multiple layers of myth that is at best <i>metaphorically</i> true. Nobody knows who wrote the texts, which are fragmentary. No methuselahs old enough to know this stuff are very talkative, and there\u2019s some indication that several of the Antefrickindiluvians, of all beings, don\u2019t even believe it. Hell, the Ministry\u2019s entire thing as a clan is rejection of Noddism and monotheism generally.<br /> <br /> Shakanaka up there ought to love the Ministry; they\u2019re in total agreement about the Caine stuff being nonsense that drags it all down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T21:36:17-07:00","id":1389845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389824#post1389824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caine myth makes sense in the setting since in Europe and America the two main sects came out of medieval Europe, so of course they saw the world through a Christianizing lens. It would be odd if they didn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>And do not forget the Cainite Heresy. When you consider that in the Real World (TM) we have had Christian heresies that thought that Christ was, somehow, the Snake in Eden...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sethianism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Zhdan_Dementiyev_01_Seth_%281630%29.jpg/960px-Zhdan_Dementiyev_01_Seth_%281630%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sethianism\" target=\"_blank\"> Sethianism - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sethianism\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sethianism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophites\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophites\" target=\"_blank\"> Ophites - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophites\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophites </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> the whole system of belief of the Sabbat and the Church of Caine look much more realistic and believable...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T21:40:49-07:00","id":1389849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389825#post1389825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you make Hinduism correct then everything else is incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, Hinduism has plenty of space to let everything else be correct and incorrect at the same time; when, preparing a Nagaraja character who had been, in life, a sadhu, I studied Shaivism a little... I discovered that the same school of belief can have monotheistic, dualistic, polytheistic and almost atheist sub-schools and all of them are... 'almost' happily living together... My head wanted to explore and go on a different life, away from my body...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T22:10:34-07:00","id":1389853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389802#post1389802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there should be completely different and unrelated vampires that only appear in areas with high concentrations of East Asian people, because Asians and their ancient mystical ways are essentially different from other... oh no, wait, it\u2019s the 21st century, and that\u2019s gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better than 'judeo Christian myth is true, everything and everyone else is a delusional idiot.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T22:13:30-07:00","id":1389854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389853#post1389853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better than 'judeo Christian myth is true, everything and everyone else is a delusional idiot.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, this is something I don't think holds water. Especially since applying it to <i>Mage: The Ascension</i>, <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>, and <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> would result in the same things applying to Christianity. It's true in the setting of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade </i>because that's the story.<br /> <br /> This is basically the reverse of a religious person complaining about <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> being biased against religious individuals. HPL created an atheist materialist universe. It should be allowed as a product of fantasy.<br /> <br /> Real cosmic answers are not inherently bad in world-building, no matter what they are. Artists should have the freedom to explore the themes and implications of their settings, in this case making Judeo-Christian themes to their vampire game just like Interview with a Vampire does (be they atheist or Catholic or maltheist depending on Anne Rice's mood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T22:20:33-07:00","id":1389856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389854#post1389854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, this is something that I think makes no sense and does not in any way shape or form hold water. Especially since applying it to Mage: The Ascension, Werewolf: The Apocalypse, and Changeling the Dreaming would result in the same things to Christianity. It's true in the setting of Vampire: The Masquerade because that's the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given some other old shame books it totally holds water. That was the attitude intended and shown, with judeo Christian myth, specifically a north European version of it being the truth, in universe, for the Vampire line. That has to die, but Ebony Kingdom reinforces that attitude, with the silly natives being wrong and the enlightened European vampires being right. As soon as you make a cultures vampires cainites, even if they don't call themselves that, you declare their myths and faiths false and delusional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T22:23:29-07:00","id":1389858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389856#post1389856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given some other old shame books it totally holds water. That was the attitude intended and shown, with judeo Christian myth, specifically a north European version of it being the truth, in universe, for the Vampire line. That has to die, but Ebony Kingdom reinforces that attitude, with the silly natives being wrong and the enlightened European vampires being right. As soon as you make a cultures vampires cainites, even if they don't call themselves that, you declare their myths and faiths false and delusional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's some uncomfortable undertones here because the largest religions of Africa are Christianity and Islam.<br /> <br /> Indeed, African Christianity is every bit as old and important culturally to it as Europe. Neither Christianity nor Islam were exported from Europe, they were brought by original disciples of Jesus and Muhammed from the Middle East. The World Book Encyclopedia has estimated that in 2002 <b>Christians</b> formed 40% of the continent's population, with Muslims forming 45%. It was also estimated in 2002 that <b>Christians</b> form 45% of <b>Africa's</b> population, with Muslims forming 40.6%.<br /> <br /> So 85% of the continent would believe in the Caine myth.<br /> <br /> Given Christianity has been in Africa for 2000 years, why is not &quot;their&quot; myth? This isn't overlaying actual African beliefs, it's acknowledging that Africans would have the legend of Cain, Nod, and the Curse centuries before most of Europe. Remember that Charlemagne was the guy who converted most of Europe to Christianity.<br /> <br /> Ethiopia's Christianization: 316 AD<br /> <br /> France's Christianitization: 596 A.D.<br /> <br /> You're basically acting like Europe &quot;owns&quot; Christianity and that's weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T22:36:44-07:00","id":1389860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389858#post1389858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given Christianity has been in Africa for 2000 years, why is not &quot;their&quot; myth? This isn't overlaying actual African beliefs, it's acknowledging that Africans would have the legend of Cain, Nod, and the Curse centuries before most of Europe. Remember that Charlemagne was the guy who converted most of Europe to Christianity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I once ran a short adventure of Mage: the Sorcerer's Crusade in Ethiopia (14... something) and it was awesome; the players (and their characters) were flabberghasted (as most of them were from the Order of Reason) but it was quite great! I didn't had time to introduce some Laibon, both bestial and otherwise and... I assure you, I had every intention to make it worthwhile their journey across the sea...<br /> <br /> Maybe I should develop it for Storyteller's Vault...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T22:47:33-07:00","id":1389866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389860#post1389860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I once ran a short adventure of Mage: the Sorcerer's Crusade in Ethiopia (14... something) and it was awesome; the players (and their characters) were flabberghasted (as most of them were from the Order of Reason) but it was quite great! I didn't had time to introduce some Laibon, both bestial and otherwise and... I assure you, I had every intention to make it worthwhile their journey across the sea...<br /> <br /> Maybe I should develop it for Storyteller's Vault...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds awesome. The Kingdom of Prester John would be an awesome Horizon Realm for the Celestial Choir and I once did a 1930s Mage game set during WW2 where we had to beat the Nazis to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:09:17-07:00","id":1389869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389858#post1389858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's some uncomfortable undertones here because the largest religions of Africa are Christianity and Islam.<br /> <br /> Indeed, African Christianity is every bit as old and important culturally to it as Europe. Neither Christianity nor Islam were exported from Europe, they were brought by original disciples of Jesus and Muhammed from the Middle East. The World Book Encyclopedia has estimated that in 2002 <b>Christians</b> formed 40% of the continent's population, with Muslims forming 45%. It was also estimated in 2002 that <b>Christians</b> form 45% of <b>Africa's</b> population, with Muslims forming 40.6%.<br /> <br /> So 85% of the continent would believe in the Caine myth.<br /> <br /> Given Christianity has been in Africa for 2000 years, why is not &amp;quot;their&amp;quot; myth? This isn't overlaying actual African beliefs, it's acknowledging that Africans would have the legend of Cain, Nod, and the Curse centuries before most of Europe. Remember that Charlemagne was the guy who converted most of Europe to Christianity.<br /> <br /> Ethiopia's Christianization: 316 AD<br /> <br /> France's Christianitization: 596 A.D.<br /> <br /> You're basically acting like Europe &amp;quot;owns&amp;quot; Christianity and that's weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, ok, I guess this in part overflow of how pissed I still am that Mithras, Odin etc are all vampires, and the denigration of those traditions, making me over sensitive to it being done to current faiths as well. Basically as soon as they tied vampires to Christianity the tied it to the massive negative connotations of that religion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:14:49-07:00","id":1389872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389869#post1389869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, ok, I guess this in part overflow of how pissed I still am that Mithras, Odin etc are all vampires, and the denigration of those traditions, making me over sensitive to it being done to current faiths as well. Basically as soon as they tied vampires to Christianity the tied it to the massive negative connotations of that religion</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are overlooking both Euhemerism (the interpretation of mythology which says that mythos are developments from real, human events) and the fact that these characters (Mithras actually, I haven't seen Odin in any Vampire sourcebook) 'say' they are the gods themselves. In fact, I would swear multiples 'copies' of Mithras and other sky and sun gods are dancing and having fun in godly ways around the Umbra in both Werewolf and Mage...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:28:22-07:00","id":1389875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389872#post1389872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think you are overlooking both Euhemerism (the interpretation of mythology which says that mythos are developments from real, human events) and the fact that these characters (Mithras actually, I haven't seen Odin in any Vampire sourcebook) 'say' they are the gods themselves. In fact, I would swear multiples 'copies' of Mithras and other sky and sun gods are dancing and having fun in godly ways around the Umbra in both Werewolf and Mage...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Gangrel Methuselah Charlatan pretending to be Odin, and he wasn't the only one a thousand years ago it was popular. But Vargr, Scandinavian vampires, have a story that Cainarl was the First Vampire after he received the blood of Odin while dying on the field of Battle.<br /> <br /> We have an older series of Stories from the Fenrir who have stories of Wotan being a Necromancer from the East, the way it was described he could have been a Wan Gui, or even of the Generation of Wan Xian that became Wan Gui. He was slain they believe he was reincarnated around the time in the Dark Ages when Fenrir was bound from the Material World. The way it was described it could also be a reference to Exalted, Odin as described by them could have been a Solar who killed Fenris' Solar Mate, and Fenris could have been a Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:53:21-07:00","id":1389880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389875#post1389875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a Gangrel Methuselah Charlatan pretending to be Odin, and he wasn't the only one a thousand years ago it was popular. But Vargr, Scandinavian vampires, have a story that Cainarl was the First Vampire after he received the blood of Odin while dying on the field of Battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, my mistake... please, where is this story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:57:49-07:00","id":1389882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389880#post1389880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, my mistake... please, where is this story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves of the Sea talks about it, a setting book for the time period a little before Vampire the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> And the Werewolf story is in the Get of Fenris Revised book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:04:06-07:00","id":1389903,"title":"","content":"This is a fascinating debate. Thanks.<br /> <br /> My personal take on the Laibon is a modified version of the creation myth in KotEK. The founder of the Laibon is a Khoikhoi shaman (not sure the right word for this) named Cogaz (I took the name from Dead Magic 2). He falls in love with the daughter of the sun god, but when she falls for his brother (Nakati) instead, he kills his brother in a jealous rage. Then the sun god curses him and transforms him into the first Laibon. Of the eleven Legacies/Lineages in the book, eight are descended from vampires Embraced by Cogaz/Cagn/whoever at different times in history. The other three are the Setites (a Cainite clan originally from Egypt), the Ishtarri (a Toreador bloodline from Mesopotamia) and the Nkulu Zao (a Salubri bloodline native to Africa).<br /> <br /> Basically, as long as your idea for the Laibon creation myth isn\u2019t blatantly ridiculous and doesn\u2019t offend any players of African ancestry in your group (or players of Asian ancestry in the case of the Wan Gui), you\u2019re good in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Random question: what does essentialist mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:09:39-07:00","id":1389905,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> interesting. You think Exalted could be the prehistory of the World of Darkness? The one guy I talked to about this irl thinks Exalted exists at the same time and in the same universe as WoD, but a very different space (his Creation is a pocket dimension surrounded by the Flux Realm, which the Exalted call the Wyld). I actually like your idea better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:17:20-07:00","id":1389906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389905#post1389905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> interesting. You think Exalted could be the prehistory of the World of Darkness? The one guy I talked to about this irl thinks Exalted exists at the same time and in the same universe as WoD, but a very different space (his Creation is a pocket dimension surrounded by the Flux Realm, which the Exalted call the Wyld). I actually like your idea better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that method using Flux as a Door has been used by others before, why people do this though is convenience because it allows a story inroad for having a fun crossover. Holden, one of the Exalted Developers actually made 2 pdfs that are Exalted vs World of Darkness, they do a hell of a job translating Exalted coming back to the World of Darkness, as in the Exaltations were imprisoned in a Black Vault in the Himalayas. It includes things that imply that Creation became prehistory sometime before 50k years ago, because they had the oldest songlines of the Aborigines of Australia, and other cavempaintings referencing Dragonblooded. It was very interesting and brilliant and free to download.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:19:02-07:00","id":1389909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389903#post1389903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fascinating debate. Thanks.<br /> <br /> My personal take on the Laibon is a modified version of the creation myth in KotEK. The founder of the Laibon is a Khoikhoi shaman (not sure the right word for this) named Cogaz (I took the name from Dead Magic 2). He falls in love with the daughter of the sun god, but when she falls for his brother (Nakati) instead, he kills his brother in a jealous rage. Then the sun god curses him and transforms him into the first Laibon. Of the eleven Legacies/Lineages in the book, eight are descended from vampires Embraced by Cogaz/Cagn/whoever at different times in history. The other three are the Setites (a Cainite clan originally from Egypt), the Ishtarri (a Toreador bloodline from Mesopotamia) and the Nkulu Zao (a Salubri bloodline native to Africa).<br /> <br /> Basically, as long as your idea for the Laibon creation myth isn\u2019t blatantly ridiculous and doesn\u2019t offend any players of African ancestry in your group (or players of Asian ancestry in the case of the Wan Gui), you\u2019re good in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Random question: what does essentialist mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love your summary, Penelope. What about the Mla Watu? Are they Laibon or Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:21:20-07:00","id":1389910,"title":"","content":"Really good question! I\u2019m not sure. They could be a Laibon Legacy or they could be a Cappadocian bloodline. Gotta think about that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:24:34-07:00","id":1389911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389903#post1389903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fascinating debate. <br /> <br /> Random question: what does essentialist mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a philologist, not an anthropologist or historian, but... This is from Wikipedia:<br /> <br /> Essentialism in history as a field of study entails discerning and listing essential cultural characteristics of a particular nation or culture, in the belief that a people or culture can be understood in this way. Sometimes such essentialism leads to claims of a praiseworthy national or cultural identity, or to its opposite, the condemnation of a culture based on presumed essential characteristics. Herodotus, for example, claims that Egyptian culture is essentially feminized and possesses a &quot;softness&quot; which has made Egypt easy to conquer.[41] To what extent Herodotus was an essentialist is a matter of debate; he is also credited with not essentializing the concept of the Athenian identity,[42] or differences between the Greeks and the Persians that are the subject of his Histories.[43]<br /> <br /> Essentialism had been operative in colonialism as well as in critiques of colonialism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:29:55-07:00","id":1389912,"title":"","content":"And thank you \ud83d\ude0a. I changed the creation myth cause I like romance and cause I wanted the first Laibon to be a tragic hero like Othello instead of a total asshole who kills his brother because he\u2019s afraid to fight that Lion creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:31:12-07:00","id":1389913,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That really helps.<br /> <br /> Now what\u2019s a philologist? lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:38:51-07:00","id":1389916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389869#post1389869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, ok, I guess this in part overflow of how pissed I still am that Mithras, Odin etc are all vampires, and the denigration of those traditions, making me over sensitive to it being done to current faiths as well. Basically as soon as they tied vampires to Christianity the tied it to the massive negative connotations of that religion</div> </div> </div> </div>I guessed it might be something like that.<br /> <br /> Vampires impersonating gods is something that I theoretically have no problem with myself as it's something that has a long fictional tradition as well as fits in with the setting's themes. However, when you get into the idea of, &quot;Pagan gods are all just evil blood cults&quot; it becomes an uncomfortable bit of cultural imperialism. Also, the idea of the vampires being the inspiration for religions that have historical or mythological significant for present-day individuals.<br /> <br /> It's also a deeply overused trope in V:TM:<br /> <br /> * Mictlantecuhtli<br /> * Hu\u012btzil\u014dp\u014dchtli (This one irritates me a lot because it's, &quot;Oh, it's a Baali!&quot;)<br /> * Quezticoatl (mage of the NWO - see above)<br /> * Odin<br /> * Tiamat<br /> * Mithras<br /> * Set<br /> * Osiris<br /> * Horus<br /> * Isis<br /> <br /> So I think I get you.<br /> <br /> I think it can be done sometimes in moderation. Helena and Menele are not actual gods (albeit tying them to Carthage makes no sense because that's 700 years after Homer). I also really enjoy the character of Mithras but there's nothing really about him that requires him to be that particular figure. A friend of mine who ran &quot;Gotham City by Night&quot; substituted the 6000 year old Kal-El based on him and it was essentially unchanged in that being an ancient vampire who deluded himself into being a Sun God (and maybe was a demigod in life) was what was important.<br /> <br /> I think the game sometimes acknowledges this too like the Children of Damballah. The Setites tried to co-opt a real snake god that is worshiped today and his followers were like, &quot;Damballah isn't evil you assholes!&quot; That was a retcon, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:50:31-07:00","id":1389919,"title":"","content":"Oddly, pointing out 8.5 out of 10 people believe in an Abrahamic religion in Africa makes me wonder if they should be going, &quot;Listen, this isn't us misunderstanding the Caine myth. You're mispronouncing his name. Also, your version of the Book of Nod is missing like 5 books. Who did this hack job?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:53:23-07:00","id":1389922,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I totally agree. Making all pagan religions \u201cevil blood cults\u201d is disgusting. Everyone I talked to agrees that Shaitan is not the real god Huitzilopochtli and that the real Huitzilopochtli hates him. If I combined WoD and Trinity Continuum I\u2019d make Quetzalcoatl a nova (in the original Trinity game there actually is an Aberrant named Feathered Serpent, so there is some textual support for this). Otherwise I\u2019d make him a proto-Dreamspeaker.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3586_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3586\" data-vbnamecard=\"3586\">Alqamar Alaswad</a> I just looked up philologist. That\u2019s awesome! I love literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:54:55-07:00","id":1389924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389913#post1389913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! That really helps.<br /> <br /> Now what\u2019s a philologist? lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ha! Someone who studies philology (in my case, English philology). Tolkien was a philologist; philology is the study of a particular language (most importantly, its 'texts'), as opposed to linguistics, which is the study of all of them and of what makes a human language a human language.<br /> <br /> (Linguistics versus philology in a nutshell for non-initiates: fellow philologists and linguists, do not kill me, please)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 05-19-2020, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:56:14-07:00","id":1389925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389922#post1389922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I totally agree. Making all pagan religions \u201cevil blood cults\u201d is disgusting. Everyone I talked to agrees that Shaitan is not the real god Huitzilopochtli and that the real Huitzilopochtli hates him. If I combined WoD and Trinity Continuum I\u2019d make Quetzalcoatl a nova (in the original Trinity game there actually is an Aberrant named Feathered Serpent, so there is some textual support for this). Otherwise I\u2019d make him a proto-Dreamspeaker.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3586_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3586\" data-vbnamecard=\"3586\">Alqamar Alaswad</a> I just looked up philologist. That\u2019s awesome! I love literature.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually does kind of make me wish they'd retcon Mictlantecuhtli as surviving the events of DIABLERIE: MEXICO. Not because he's the inspiration for the figure necessarily, just because if he is the vampire impersonating him that he should have a bit more importance historically and regionally than being the dragon at the end of the dungeon.<br /> <br /> Make him a figure of the Drowned.<br /> <br /> Right now, it's a little too much, &quot;The Drowned have no NPCs and thus are a nebulous force versus being a valid faction of vampires in their own right.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:56:49-07:00","id":1389926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389919#post1389919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, pointing out 8.5 out of 10 people believe in an Abrahamic religion in Africa makes me wonder if they should be going, &quot;Listen, this isn't us misunderstanding the Caine myth. You're mispronouncing his name. Also, your version of the Book of Nod is missing like 5 books. Who did this hack job?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be awesome; a handful of elder Laibon arrives to... a meeting of Camarilla scholars, take out a handful of facsimile and digital copies of ancient papyrus (papyruses?) and scrolls and says what you are saying: &quot;Ah, we have discovered that Caine was African all along and that your Book of Nod is really a falsification and that you are missing... let me see... five tomes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T04:06:44-07:00","id":1389930,"title":"","content":"Oh interesting perspective academically speaking, haven't talked to philogists since Uni. :P Just wish more people I met in College liked White Wolf games rather then WoW and DnD. :P<br /> <br /> I like your timelines and reimagines of history Penelope.<br /> <br /> Its interesting because the World of Darkness uses a mix and match of which beings are the literal gods, which inspired gods, and which are wearing them as masks.<br /> <br /> The Analects of the Third Garden even has some nice easter eggs for both Wan Gui and Xi Dundu. And the Kinyonyi may be the only branch of Ravnos unaffected by the Death Frenzy of Zapathsura's curse.<br /> <br /> And its interesting how the Guruhi are tied to switching between Divine regality and abhorrent horror. They may indeed be descendants of Absimiliard before he fell to his wretched self loathing. They became the first kings outside the Cities of Caine because he was the greatest Hunter and was beautiful of continence so they they have Presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> It would have been so fun to have had the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom kick off as a spin off gameline like Kindred of the East. Now they only have their corebook and some mentions in the Jyhad Diary and a few Bloodlines in Dark Age Vampire 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T04:16:04-07:00","id":1389931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389926#post1389926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be awesome; a handful of elder Laibon arrives to... a meeting of Camarilla scholars, take out a handful of facsimile and digital copies of ancient papyrus (papyruses?) and scrolls and says what you are saying: &quot;Ah, we have discovered that Caine was African all along and that your Book of Nod is really a falsification and that you are missing... let me see... five tomes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that seems to be a perfectly valid adventure hook that doesn't contradict any of the canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T05:33:01-07:00","id":1389937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389916#post1389916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guessed it might be something like that.<br /> <br /> Vampires impersonating gods is something that I theoretically have no problem with myself as it's something that has a long fictional tradition as well as fits in with the setting's themes. However, when you get into the idea of, &quot;Pagan gods are all just evil blood cults&quot; it becomes an uncomfortable bit of cultural imperialism. Also, the idea of the vampires being the inspiration for religions that have historical or mythological significant for present-day individuals.<br /> <br /> It's also a deeply overused trope in V:TM:<br /> <br /> * Mictlantecuhtli<br /> * Hu\u012btzil\u014dp\u014dchtli (This one irritates me a lot because it's, &quot;Oh, it's a Baali!&quot;)<br /> * Quezticoatl (mage of the NWO - see above)<br /> * Odin<br /> * Tiamat<br /> * Mithras<br /> * Set<br /> * Osiris<br /> * Horus<br /> * Isis<br /> <br /> So I think I get you.<br /> <br /> I think it can be done sometimes in moderation. Helena and Menele are not actual gods (albeit tying them to Carthage makes no sense because that's 700 years after Homer). I also really enjoy the character of Mithras but there's nothing really about him that requires him to be that particular figure. A friend of mine who ran &quot;Gotham City by Night&quot; substituted the 6000 year old Kal-El based on him and it was essentially unchanged in that being an ancient vampire who deluded himself into being a Sun God (and maybe was a demigod in life) was what was important.<br /> <br /> I think the game sometimes acknowledges this too like the Children of Damballah. The Setites tried to co-opt a real snake god that is worshiped today and his followers were like, &quot;Damballah isn't evil you assholes!&quot; That was a retcon, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it's not wanting what feels like every single non-Abrahamic faith turning out to be a Vampire cult in disguise. About the only way I can see of doing that is to make them as true in universe as the Abrahamic faiths, and that in this case involves their cultural/religious myths being demonstrably true....which means, new vampires not related to Cainites in origin or powers. (And then you can have the real fun metaphysical Consensus arguments, and start talking about Paradigms etc etc) (For instance if I was doing it for Old Norse faiths it would be people rising after death as Draugr, animated by sheer will, hideous walking corpses, with a list of magic powers and some shape shifting, motivated by hunger, jealousy and greed. No sire, no clans, revenants animated not by a curse, but by the corpses own spirit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-19-2020, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T05:48:04-07:00","id":1389940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389937#post1389937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, it's not wanting what feels like every single non-Abrahamic faith turning out to be a Vampire cult in disguise. About the only way I can see of doing that is to make them as true in universe as the Abrahamic faiths, and that in this case involves their cultural/religious myths being demonstrably true....which means, new vampires not related to Cainites in origin or powers. (And then you can have the real fun metaphysical Consensus arguments, and start talking about Paradigms etc etc) (For instance if I was doing it for Old Norse faiths it would be people rising after death as Draugr, animated by sheer will, hideous walking corpses, with a list of magic powers and some shape shifting, motivated by hunger, jealousy and greed. No sire, no clans, revenants animated not by a curse, but by the corpses own spirit)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the World of Darkness that's already true with the Umbra full of all the gods that vampires impersonate. However, I've stated that I think it can also just be the premise of the game that a certain mythology or worldview is true because that's the game. It's not a big deal if a roleplaying game makes that as its not real people being affected.<br /> <br /> In Nomine doesn't have to be ecumenical.<br /> <br /> Neither does Call of Cthulhu have to be pro-religious.<br /> <br /> But you should do what makes you feel good at your table, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T05:51:18-07:00","id":1389941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389919#post1389919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, pointing out 8.5 out of 10 people believe in an Abrahamic religion in Africa makes me wonder if they should be going, &quot;Listen, this isn't us misunderstanding the Caine myth. You're mispronouncing his name. Also, your version of the Book of Nod is missing like 5 books. Who did this hack job?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had somewhat similar ideas before about Noddist texts being misinterpreted and mistranslated at various points, and were actually much longer and based on something more akin to the Werewolf mythology. Abrahamic kindred saw the title 'shaper' and see their own conclusions from that.<br /> <br /> They idea is that the original version was along the lines of 'long ago at the dawn of agriculture a farmer ended up possessed by a spirit of the Destroyer (Wyrm), and their first act under the possession was to kill their signing and drink their blood. When the Shaper (Weaver) saw this she was distraught, and cursed the farmer with eternal statis and a hunger for blood'.<br /> <br /> I really do like the idea that the Laibon would have a different set of Noddist texts which shared similarities and differences. Have the creation myth differ slightly, give 'Caine' some new deeds that don't appear in the will known fragments, and have absolutely no mention of some key element of European Noddism (I vote the Second City).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 05-19-2020, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:00:30-07:00","id":1389942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389940#post1389940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the World of Darkness that's already true with the Umbra full of all the gods that vampires impersonate. However, I've stated that I think it can also just be the premise of the game that a certain mythology or worldview is true because that's the game. It's not a big deal if a roleplaying game makes that as its not real people being affected.<br /> <br /> In Nomine doesn't have to be ecumenical.<br /> <br /> Neither does Call of Cthulhu have to be pro-religious.<br /> <br /> But you should do what makes you feel good at your table, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Nomines entire premise is religious, (And I can avoid it for that reason, and do) <br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu's entire premise is, again, openly about Elder things and Cthonic Deities, avoid it if you want<br /> <br /> VtMs Premise is being about Vampires...and then you find out later it's only Vampires based on Christian Myth, no other Vampires are real, most other religions are blood cults and thus totally invalid and only followed by mentally deficient members of inferior cultures, whose ancestors where suckered by the superior creatures of abrahamic myth. If the game was open with being Abrahamic-supremacist, that would be one thing, but it claims to be about Vampires......yea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:05:11-07:00","id":1389946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389942#post1389942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Nomines entire premise is religious, (And I can avoid it for that reason, and do)<br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu's entire premise is, again, openly about Elder things and Cthonic Deities, avoid it if you want<br /> <br /> VtMs Premise is being about Vampires...and then you find out later it's only Vampires based on Christian Myth, no other Vampires are real, most other religions are blood cults and thus totally invalid and only followed by mentally deficient members of inferior cultures, whose ancestors where suckered by the superior creatures of abrahamic myth. If the game was open with being Abrahamic-supremacist, that would be one thing, but it claims to be about Vampires......yea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its ultimately how we view it.<br /> <br /> For me, the entire premise of all three games is to be an enjoyable game. Religious elements incorporated into it are part of the game primarily versus any religious content itself. The purpose of the game is to have fun, which the religious content is a part of. It's also notable because In Nomine started as an anti-Catholic religious comedy but got remade to a more respectful version by Steve Jackson games.<br /> <br /> But basically, you seem to have a severe issue with the fact the premise of the game is that it is explictly tied to Judeo-Christian mythology in its fundamentals as a worldbuilding element. To me, this is like complaining that Dragonlance is all about Paladine vs. Takhasis. Its laser-focused on an element that too much is being read into that can't be removed from the story because it's the foundation of it. It's not a political statement, IMHO, but the art itself and themes.<br /> <br /> Which is, &quot;Vampire is richer for it being tied to the Caine myth and you can't remove it or dilute it without causing the whole thing to collapse any more than Werewolf would be by introducing the Judeo-Christian God&quot; on a purely artistic/storytelling basis. You can't add God to HPL's Cthulhu Mythos without screwing it up and you can't add Odin to Lord of the Rings.<br /> <br /> Still, it may just be preference and I could be unconsciously biased because I am a progressive religious person in RL. That may be influencing my appreciation of said content in the game.<br /> <br /> You are 100% welcome to disagree but I think a single origin for all vampires is the best way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:20:48-07:00","id":1389950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389853#post1389853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better than 'judeo Christian myth is true, everything and everyone else is a delusional idiot.'</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that logically follow on any level? In order for this objection to make sense, the Caine myth would have to be the objective, literal truth of the setting (which it almost certainly isn\u2019t), and yet somehow <i>not </i>the truth at the same time. Because if it were the literal Word-of-God origin for one group of vampires, then it would be true in the setting. Having an unrelated group of vampires that it doesn\u2019t pertain to wouldn\u2019t then make it untrue.<br /> <br /> But none of that matters because (<i>once more with feeling</i>) the Caine myth as modern vampires have received it is <i>not </i>the literal, objective, Word-of-God origin of vampires and never was. It\u2019s a mythic narrative European vampires have used to rationalize their existence within their cultural context, and using quasi-Christian themes to express the anxieties at the heart of their existence. Other groups of vampires \u2014 demonstrably the same species \u2014 have other narratives, and vampire culture predates Judaism in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:22:42-07:00","id":1389952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389950#post1389950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does that logically follow on any level? In order for this objection to make sense, the Caine myth would have to be the objective, literal truth of the setting (which it almost certainly isn\u2019t), and yet somehow <i>not </i>the truth at the same time. Because if it were the literal Word-of-God origin for one group of vampires, then it would be true in the setting. Having an unrelated group of vampires that it doesn\u2019t pertain to wouldn\u2019t then make it untrue.<br /> <br /> But none of that matters because (<i>once more with feeling</i>) the Caine myth as modern vampires have received it is <i>not </i>the literal, objective, Word-of-God origin of vampires and never was. It\u2019s a mythic narrative European vampires have used to rationalize their existence within their cultural context, and using quasi-Christian themes to express the anxieties at the heart of their existence. Other groups of vampires \u2014 demonstrably the same species \u2014 have other narratives, and vampire culture predates Judaism in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it's a little weird because the view of God, Caine, Satan, and Lilith in the Vampire setting tends to be maltheist and certainly not-Pro Christianity. After all, the Book of Nod has Caine sacrifice Able versus murdering him over jealousy. Oh and God unleashed a horrifying plague on humanity by creating vampires. Thanks YVHS.<br /> <br /> This is all off-topic, though, and we might want to consider a new thread if we want to discuss religious themes in vampire (and are very very polite about it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:29:42-07:00","id":1389953,"title":"","content":"Regarding the presentation of vampires as pagan gods, it could have been handled better, definitely. I can buy that a vampire would take the identity of a god for their own purposes and might get a lot of mileage out of that, but if the setting starts to imply that humans can\u2019t come up with their own mythic/religious traditions without vampiric interference, then it\u2019s part of the larger problem of all of human civilization being the product of vampires, which is dumb. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the idea that Christianity got a pass somehow, or that the setting is Abrahamic-supremacist just doesn\u2019t hold water. In that case the Christian church wouldn\u2019t be largely a pet project of the Lasombra, and the quasi-Abrahamic vampire religions wouldn\u2019t be so overtly heretical and depraved. Also, you know, if there\u2019s a Yahweh up there on his throne overseeing the WoD, he\u2019s obviously not good for much. It\u2019s just that the game plays with the dominant cultural trends and mythic imagery of its default setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:31:17-07:00","id":1389954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389953#post1389953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the presentation of vampires as pagan gods, it could have been handled better, definitely. I can buy that a vampire would take the identity of a god for their own purposes and might get a lot of mileage out of that, but if the setting starts to imply that humans can\u2019t come up with their own mythic/religious traditions without vampiric interference, then it\u2019s part of the larger problem of all of human civilization being the product of vampires, which is dumb.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the idea that Christianity got a pass somehow, or that the setting is Abrahamic-supremacist just doesn\u2019t hold water. In that case the Christian church wouldn\u2019t be largely a pet project of the Lasombra, and the quasi-Abrahamic vampire religions wouldn\u2019t be so overtly heretical and depraved. Also, you know, if there\u2019s a Yahweh up there on his throne overseeing the WoD, he\u2019s obviously not good for much. It\u2019s just that the game plays with the dominant cultural trends and mythic imagery of its default setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best summary is to think of religion in V:TM as &quot;Goth&quot; rather than Judeo-Christian. It was created out of the Atlanta sub culture that was specifically reactionary to the Bible Belt.<br /> <br /> There's a reason that vampires are Damned after all and that's taking the view, &quot;Well, if I am, then what do I do about it? I know, PARTY LIKE ITS 1992!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:38:08-07:00","id":1389955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389954#post1389954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the best summary is to think of religion in V:TM as &quot;Goth&quot; rather than Judeo-Christian. It was created out of the Atlanta sub culture that was specifically reactionary to the Bible Belt.<br /> <br /> There's a reason that vampires are Damned after all and that's taking the view, &quot;Well, if I am, then what do I do about it? I know, PARTY LIKE ITS 1992!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We\u2019re in agreement there. I\u2019m reminded of the cathedral nightclub in the Bloodlines video game. Gothic churches, crosses, cemeteries, etc., have religious significance, but for vampires it\u2019s mostly the aesthetic that\u2019s important. <br /> <br /> It makes me wonder what goth subculture would look like in an Islamic context. It seems to me that would have some relevance for the visual aesthetic of not just the Banu Haqim, but also the Laibon. Africa is largely Muslim, after all, despite a significant Christian minority. And even among African Christians, I don\u2019t know how much the standard gothic aesthetic makes sense in context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T09:24:08-07:00","id":1389986,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> as a former goth (some of my friends still are), I totally agree with you guys, especially about the aesthetic. I also don\u2019t think V:tM is Abrahamic-centered at all.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a real club near where I live that is a lot like the one in Bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T09:33:31-07:00","id":1389988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389916#post1389916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It becomes an uncomfortable bit of cultural imperialism. Also, the idea of the vampires being the inspiration for religions that have historical or mythological significant for present-day individuals.<br /> <br /> * Hu\u012btzil\u014dp\u014dchtli (This one irritates me a lot because it's, &amp;quot;Oh, it's a Baali!&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This one didn\u2019t bother me because;<br /> <br /> A) it wasn\u2019t A Baali, it was THE Baali... the first one to appear in the World of Darkness and introduced us to the very concept of the Baali.<br /> <br /> B) Cultural Imperialism isn\u2019t just a Western European thing. The Aztecs were also colonial oppressors who moved into and conquered the region in the 13th Century CE (only about 300 years ahead of the Spanish Conquistadors) and began sacrificing members of the conquered peoples to their gods in what was arguably a political terror campaign dressed up as religious fanaticism.<br /> <br /> Frankly, them being in the thrall to an actual 10,000 year old demonic blood god makes them look better than they actually were... in the real world they committed those atrocities of their free will.<br /> <br /> One thing that often gets scrubbed out of the story is that Cort\u00e9s didn\u2019t go to war with the Aztecs and beat them with just his 500 men; he negotiated alliances with local conquered peoples who sent along armies in the thousands to assist Cort\u00e9s in overthrowing the Aztecs. The Spanish conquest wasn\u2019t good, but at the time, Cort\u00e9s was considered the lesser of two evils compared to the Aztecs.<br /> <br /> At the same time I do feel that there\u2019s a bit of a double standard regarding religion in fantasy. If a Christian has an issue with a fantasy setting where, say, the Norse religion was objectively true, they\u2019re expected to just accept it as part of the fantasy setting. If a non-Christian has an issue with a fantasy setting where Christianity is objectively true though, the expectation is that the Christian setting must be changed to not be problematic.<br /> <br /> VtM was specifically built on Judeo-Christian cosmology. WtA was built on an animist cosmology. MtA was built on a variation of Gnostic cosmology. CtD is based more on the pre-Christian myths of the British Isles. WtO is, if anything, an agnostic to even atheistic setting.<br /> <br /> DtF is also Judeo-Christian, but given that Dante\u2019s Inferno and Paradise Lost are two of the most defining works of popular literature relating to demons and, more importantly to the WoD brand, one of the few cosmologies where demons are presented as unambiguous monsters (vs. say, the Greek conception of daemons as being a general category of supernatural being that might be helpful or harmful depending on the daemon).<br /> <br /> The point being; if you really believe that Christianity is just a myth no different than the Greco-Roman pantheon; then the use of it as the foundation for a fantasy setting should be no more problematic than one where the Greek gods are presumed to be real (ex. Perry Jackson; and therefore Christianity is objectively false in that setting).<br /> <br /> Especially when WW only used the Christian cosmology for one of the big three with the other two outright rejecting it as true. That paints the picture of Christianity in VtM being a conscious choice based on the primary source material (most notably the novel that kicked off the whole vampire in popular culture in the first place; \u201cDracula\u201d) than some sort of deliberate attempt to exclude (if that were the case one would expect WtA and MtA to also have underlying Christian cosmologies).<br /> <br /> And just to be clear on my argument in relation to the Kindred and Laibon... whoever the first vampire was, they probably originated in Africa along with the earliest humans (probably 100-200k years ago) and so would be a common ancestor to both Kindred and Laibon. Further, since their true identity has been last to history, this first vampire may as well be called \u201cCaine\u201d when speaking of them in the English language in the same way that our most recent common mitochondrial ancestor is called \u201cEve.\u201d<br /> <br /> One thing that helps me in this regard is that the Catholic Church doesn\u2019t proclaim a literal interpretation of the earliest books of the Bible.<br /> <br /> What they teach IS true is God as Creator of the cosmos (he may have done so by setting up the conditions of the Big Bang so that our sun and planet would form and evolution would eventually produce mankind) and the relationship of God and Man (i.e. a loving creator contrary to the Babylonian religion during the time the Bible was written down where Man was spawned from the blood of demons and therefore only worthy to serve the gods and their priest-kings as slaves). All the rest can be allegories and \u201cjust so\u201d stories that explain why certain things are so.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is that, regardless of when it is actually written down, every ancient religion references events from much earlier periods that came down to them in the form of oral tradition. The nigh universal to all cultures story of a prehistoric Flood, for example, almost certainly descends from oral histories dating back to the end of the last glacial maximum and subsequent rapid rise of global sea level by 100+ meters in a very short span of time that occurred in stages between 14k and 8k years ago).<br /> <br /> Even if only got recorded in the Hebrew Torah during the Babylonian captivity c. 600-539 BCE, the oral histories recorded were at least 5500 years older in the case of the Flood, and the oldest recorded part of the Bible (the song sung after the parting of the Red Sea... which speaks only of the horses and chariots of the enemy being cast into the sea by God rather than of them being trapped there as the parting of the sea ended) was 1000 years old by the time the Torah was actually assembled.<br /> <br /> The point being, just because it only got written down about 2600 years ago, doesn\u2019t mean the foundations of the stories recorded in them are only 2600 years old.<br /> <br /> So, in the case of Caine, all that really needs to be true is that there was a First Vampire (called Caine for convenience) who came into being contemporaneously with early humans (i.e. he was a descendant of \u201cAdam &amp; Eve\u201d and \u201cCaine\u201d in turn sired other vampires who preyed on early human settlements.<br /> <br /> Maybe the story was backwards and Caine only murdered his brother after he became a vampire (a new vampire killing a loved one in their first hunger-fueled frenzy isn\u2019t exactly rare), but regardless, Caine\u2019s association with the murder of his loved one is at least an allegorical truth of the vampiric condition.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a Flood of some type almost certainly occurred for the reasons given above... but the really relevant part is what it signifies for the vampires. The Flood is the point when all contact with and involvement of \u201cCaine\u201d in human and vampire history ends.<br /> <br /> Whether this is because \u201cCaine\u201d deliberately turned his back on his childer -or- because Caine suffered torpor and the body was lost in the flood; buried under 8000+ years of sediment with no blood to restore it -or- because Caine met Final Death when the flood washed away any protection during daylight doesn\u2019t matter.<br /> <br /> What matters is precisely that everything before the Flood doesn\u2019t matter... as the oldest recorded histories begin it is the Clan founders who take the reins. Whether Caine\u2019s existence happened exactly as recorded in the Book of Nod or as the Laibon say it did is an academic argument because he\u2019s gone from the story until the last days (and maybe not even then).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T09:45:20-07:00","id":1389992,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> Yes, but it\u2019s a fascinating academic argument. Much more interesting than what I\u2019m supposed to be doing \ud83d\ude0a.<br /> <br /> Not the Catholic Church, but a certain well-known Protestant church holds a seminar every year on \u201cHow Dinosaurs and the Word of God as Revealed in Genesis Can Both Be Literally True.\u201d<br /> <br /> Also, Christianity and the Olympians can coexist. Just look at Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:06:41-07:00","id":1389996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389986#post1389986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a real club near where I live that is a lot like the one in Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. I\u2019m not really a clubgoer \u2014 and <i>definitely </i>not a churchgoer \u2014 but I might make an exception if I lived near that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T11:31:46-07:00","id":1390007,"title":"","content":"Concerning the direction this thread is going, I really, really think that the reason there are almost no info or any sourcebooks set in the 1st century of the Common Era in Jerusalem and neighbouring areas is that having a Kindred proclaiming that he is Odin (as seems to be the case in Wolves of the Sea) has almost no risk of sending hordes of thousand of people enraged to demand compensation at the doors of Onyx Path or Paradox.<br /> <br /> Were things otherwise, I am really sure Flavius Josephus, Pontio Pilates and other characters around the first centuries of Christianity would have already been depicted in some sourcebook or other... Uhmmm... Food for thought...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 05-19-2020, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T11:37:56-07:00","id":1390009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389858#post1389858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's some uncomfortable undertones here because the largest religions of Africa are Christianity and Islam.<br /> <br /> Indeed, African Christianity is every bit as old and important culturally to it as Europe. Neither Christianity nor Islam were exported from Europe, they were brought by original disciples of Jesus and Muhammed from the Middle East. The World Book Encyclopedia has estimated that in 2002 <b>Christians</b> formed 40% of the continent's population, with Muslims forming 45%. It was also estimated in 2002 that <b>Christians</b> form 45% of <b>Africa's</b> population, with Muslims forming 40.6%.<br /> <br /> So 85% of the continent would believe in the Caine myth.<br /> <br /> Given Christianity has been in Africa for 2000 years, why is not &quot;their&quot; myth? This isn't overlaying actual African beliefs, it's acknowledging that Africans would have the legend of Cain, Nod, and the Curse centuries before most of Europe. Remember that Charlemagne was the guy who converted most of Europe to Christianity.<br /> <br /> Ethiopia's Christianization: 316 AD<br /> <br /> France's Christianitization: 596 A.D.<br /> <br /> You're basically acting like Europe &quot;owns&quot; Christianity and that's weird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First of all Christianity at large came into Africa with colonization. The only place in Africa that was &quot;naturally&quot; Christian for centuries was Abyssinia (Ethiopia) and while quite a large Kingdom in terms in landmass on its own, it was only a smackdab portion of the continent. It doesn't represent the majority of the continent at all. Christianity hasn't been significant at all until European prostelyzation. Same with Islam before Berbers and Arabs started doing &quot;missionary&quot; work. Before all these Abrahamic religions even were a smidgen of a thought, the various sub-saharan tribes/nations believed in their naturalist local beliefs. Also Noddism in the context of oWoD purely came from Europe.. the Laibon don't have this as they were active much later and then congruently with the &quot;western&quot; Kindred before the Camarilla or Anarch revolt took place. The Laibon explicitly detest Abrahamic religions because it conflicts with the spiritual beliefs THEY have and they don't like the fact that their mortal population has been converted. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind the large portion of Christianity in Africa was from the Imperial age in the continent from the 19th century and up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T11:43:50-07:00","id":1390010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390007#post1390007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the direction this thread is going, I really, really think that the reason there are almost no material set in the 1st century of the Common Era in Jerusalem and neighbouring areas is that having a Kindred proclaiming that he is Odin (as seems to be the case in Wolves of the Sea) has almost no risk of sending hordes of thousand of people enraged to demand compensation at the doors of Onyx Path or Paradox.<br /> <br /> Were things otherwise, I am really sure Flavius Josephus, Pontio Pilates and other characters would have already been depicted in some sourcebook or other... Uhmmm... Food for thought...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if the Cainite Heresy and the Book of Nod didn't do it, I don't expect anything would. The hobby is too small and inconsequential for hordes of thousands of angry religious people to even know it exists, much less maintain their ire for long enough to organize anything significant.<br /> <br /> It's not like the WoD has been tiptoeing on eggshells around Christianity or anything. I think the main reason not to want to do it is that Jesus works better as a mythic figure in the setting that various cults can interpret in different ways, rather than having a book come out and say &quot;yeah, he was a Malkavian,&quot; which would be cheap and not especially useful for gaming purposes. I mean, yes, early WoD stuff <i>did </i>have moments like this, but they're not the moments we think of fondly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T11:59:50-07:00","id":1390011,"title":"","content":"In fact I wasn't thinking about Jesus himself... I was thinking about the Apostles... But yes, I really agree with you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:01:19-07:00","id":1390012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390009#post1390009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all Christianity at large came into Africa with colonization. The only place in Africa that was &quot;naturally&quot; Christian for centuries was Abyssinia (Ethiopia) and while quite a large Kingdom in terms in landmass on its own, it was only a smackdab portion of the continent. It doesn't represent the majority of the continent at all. Christianity hasn't been significant at all until European prostelyzation. Same with Islam before Berbers and Arabs started doing &quot;missionary&quot; work. Before all these Abrahamic religions even were a smidgen of a thought, the various sub-saharan tribes/nations believed in their naturalist local beliefs. Also Noddism in the context of oWoD purely came from Europe.. the Laibon don't have this as they were active much later and then congruently with the &quot;western&quot; Kindred before the Camarilla or Anarch revolt took place. The Laibon explicitly detest Abrahamic religions because it conflicts with the spiritual beliefs THEY have and they don't like the fact that their mortal population has been converted.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind the large portion of Christianity in Africa was from the Imperial age in the continent from the 19th century and up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, don't take this the wrong way but this is completely wrong.<br /> <br /> Just as a general note:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only place in Africa that was &quot;naturally&quot; Christian for centuries was Abyssinia (Ethiopia) and while quite a large Kingdom in terms in landmass on its own, it was only a smackdab portion of the continent. </div> </div> </div>* You've literally just dismissed the existence of the entire Coptic Christian church. The Church of Alexandria, in Egypt, dates back to 47 A.D. The Coptic Church is massive to this day in Egypt and other parts of Africa with as rich a history as the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox Churches.<br /> * You've dismissed the existence of the Church of Sudan. Nubian Christianity dates back to the 1st century A.D.<br /> <br /> Also, we're stretching the definition of European Christianity I think if we're going to dismiss the entire existence of the Byzantine Empire that was a massive influence on the trade and culture of North Africa. It's also dismissive to basically ignore the massive chunks of &quot;European&quot; church that were controlled and maintained locally even while giving nominal allegiance to Rome like the nation of Maghred a.k.a The Barbary Coast a.k.a The Entire Western Coast of North Africa.<br /> <br /> * We've mentioned Ethiopia already and that's a large chunk of the country as is.<br /> <br /> This strain of Christianity continued to persist after the Muslim conquest of Northern Africa but I'm confused by your use of air quotes regarding &quot;Naturally&quot; and &quot;Missionary&quot; work. Yes, I think we can all understand that new religions come in and out of fashion with the fall of governments. Is there any religion in the entire history of man which hasn't been benefited by or not benefited by the relationship with war or relationship with governments.<br /> <br /> Dismissing the role of Islam in the history of Africa is like dismissing Buddhism's role in Japanese history or, since it's been there for over a thousand years, Christianity in say Denmark.<br /> <br /> It also engages in category &quot;traitor&quot; status that is something I've always felt appalling and tied to toxic nationalism. When the King of Zimbabwe was baptized by Jesuits, the power relationships are completely within him since it's only by his order they weren't killed for a century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:07:44-07:00","id":1390014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390010#post1390010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if the Cainite Heresy and the Book of Nod didn't do it, I don't expect anything would. The hobby is too small and inconsequential for hordes of thousands of angry religious people to even know it exists, much less maintain their ire for long enough to organize anything significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's occasionally caught the attempt by Far Right groups trying to drum up controversy to increase the money at the collection plate and distract from their naked support of looter capitalism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not like the WoD has been tiptoeing on eggshells around Christianity or anything. I think the main reason not to want to do it is that Jesus works better as a mythic figure in the setting that various cults can interpret in different ways, rather than having a book come out and say &quot;yeah, he was a Malkavian,&quot; which would be cheap and not especially useful for gaming purposes. I mean, yes, early WoD stuff <i>did </i>have moments like this, but they're not the moments we think of fondly. </div> </div> </div>The irony is you're already wrong as the Followers of Set 1st Edition Clan Book pretty much states that Jesus was Set. I shit you not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There's also &quot;The Great Prank&quot; by the Malkavians. The edginess of White Wolf was a selling point for those who felt oppressed by the conformity of Southern and middle class white culture of the Nineties.<br /> <br /> Especially LGBT teens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390011#post1390011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact I wasn't thinking about Jesus himself... I was thinking about the Apostles... But yes, I really agree with you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> .</div> </div> </div> </div>To add a different perspective, I grew up in the North of the Bible Belt. They're not looking at the specifics of tabletop roleplaying games when criticizing them. They begin at, &quot;Magic&quot;, &quot;Vampires&quot;, &quot;Heavy Metal&quot;, and &quot;Wearing lots of black while having a bad attitude&quot; then end up at &quot;Satanism.&quot; The discussion of the role of Gnosticism and heresy in Catholicism in The Cainite Heresy never is going to have them devote enough attention to criticize it. They're not interested in anything beyond a surface level reading of this stuff.<br /> <br /> Harry Potter is forbidden to Far Right Christians and for profit ministries looking to line their wallet with cheap controversy. Honest intellectual discourse is not of interest to them.<br /> <br /> The only time I was ever suspended from school was bringing my V:TM books to school. The Prinicple, I shit you not, turned out to have faked his identity and credentials. He was a conman who ended up founded out by a DUI.<br /> <br /> Despite being a conservative Christian (I'm now a Far Left liberal one) at the time, I sadly lost a good friend whose church staged an intervention so he was forced to burn his &quot;Satanic&quot; books. The game line was <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i>. They brainwashed him into believing it was interfering with his faith. I was horrified by it. BOOK BURNING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:11:51-07:00","id":1390016,"title":"","content":"Wow... I'm sorry to hear that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T12:18:51-07:00","id":1390021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390016#post1390016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow... I'm sorry to hear that...</div> </div> </div> </div>It helped me reevaluate my p