y Abrahamic, and use Judeo-Christian when I think that is where an attitude comes from (mostly I slip sometimes, but at least I have tried to stay academic). Oh and my prior experience with Christianity was New Life Baptist, up until my mid teens...that's a whole bag full of crazy.<br /> <br /> Oh also 'advanced civilisation' be careful of that idea, their are reasons populations reach certain equalibriums with the environment, and so called advanced civilizations can get tanned hollow by situations so called primitive view as mundane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-19-2020, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:39:24-07:00","id":1390123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390120#post1390120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do remember, which is why I say Abrahamic, and use Judeo-Christian when I think that is where an attitude comes from (mostly I slip sometimes, but at least I have tried to stay academic). Oh and my prior experience with Christianity was New Life Baptist, up until my mid teens...that's a whole bag full of crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you did remember.<br /> <br /> Also, having grown up in the Bible Belt as I mentioned, I also have encountered some very batshit sects and individuals hiding their darker qualities behind religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:49:48-07:00","id":1390125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390123#post1390123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes you did remember.<br /> <br /> Also, having grown up in the Bible Belt as I mentioned, I also have encountered some very batshit sects and individuals hiding their darker qualities behind religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal favourite for 'insane things Sunday school said' was having the 'kill the entire city for one unbeliever' part of Deutoronomy (maybe Leviticus, either or) pointed out, and it stated that our goal should be to have kids, and raise them in isolation so they could fulfil that command this was at a UK faith camp with thousands of kids..yea. <br /> <br /> Anyway back on topic: Taggies Take, unify the WoD by having hungry dead as part of regional Consensus, bring everything under the Umbra and Paradigm milieu, don't endorse/condem any living faiths.<br /> <br /> Demon is a whole nother problem, but you can roll Mummy, Risen and KotE, as well as Liches into a Risen and peckish camp, pick exactly what they crave, assign powers, and go about telling stories, like the old Sorcery books, with added society splats. Throw that lot at the wall, see what sticks, print more for what does, throw the rest to the Vault bish bash job done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-19-2020, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T18:05:06-07:00","id":1390136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390125#post1390125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My personal favourite for 'insane things Sunday school said' was having the 'kill the entire city for one unbeliever' part of Deutoronomy (maybe Leviticus, either or) pointed out, and it stated that our goal should be to have kids, and raise them in isolation so they could fulfil that command this was at a UK faith camp with thousands of kids..yea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not even surprised. Not far from here, we had a guy faking miracles in order to get people to venerate Trump as God's Chosen King.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/02/oil-bible-dalton-georgia-trump-prophecy-evangelical-miracle.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://slate.com/human-interest/202...l-miracle.html</a><br /> <br /> Ideology is a drug. It can cure or kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway back on topic: Taggies Take, unify the WoD by having hungry dead as part of regional Consensus, bring everything under the Umbra and Paradigm milieu, don't endorse/condem any living faiths.<br /> <br /> Demon is a whole nother problem, but you can roll Mummy, Risen and KotE, as well as Liches into a Risen and peckish camp, pick exactly what they crave, assign powers, and go about telling stories, like the old Sorcery books, with added society splats. Throw that lot at the wall, see what sticks, print more for what does, throw the rest to the Vault bish bash job done. </div> </div> </div>Well, you do you man. The most important rule at any table should be that you have fun and enjoy your game whether as a player or ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2020, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T18:21:11-07:00","id":1390140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1389942#post1389942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtMs Premise is being about Vampires...and then you find out later it's only Vampires based on Christian Myth, no other Vampires are real, most other religions are blood cults and thus totally invalid and only followed by mentally deficient members of inferior cultures, whose ancestors where suckered by the superior creatures of abrahamic myth. If the game was open with being Abrahamic-supremacist, that would be one thing, but it claims to be about Vampires......yea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see a lot of posts on this forum like this, but I never had a problem like this. I don't think the game forces you to adopt Christianity or Abrahamic religion as objectively true. The fact that vampires ascribe their origins to a &quot;Caine&quot; is meaningless. While it makes total sense that Europeans in the Middle Ages would ascribe their origin to Cain, who was thought to be the father of many monsters, it would be absolutely ludicrous to think vampires from a pre-Christian tradition would ever think that to attribute their origins on the Holy Book of a small tribe of Jews. Especially those who were created before the Jewish people or the Kingdom of Israel ever existed. Obviously vampires in ancient Sumeria would NOT ascribe their origins to Cain. They would use another placeholder. And neither would the Classical Greeks or the early Romans.<br /> <br /> Do you really think that Lucian, the NPC Gangrel vampire who marched with Julius Caesar, and was literally in the first edition of the corebook, was told by his sire that the origin of vampires lies in the text of the Jewish people, who were a recent and marginal acquisition of the Roman Empire during this lifetime?<br /> <br /> There are only a few essential elements that need to occur (and even this is debateable), and any other details are simply flavor text. You need an antedeluvian world. You need a Deluge. And you need someone to be the original vampire that spawned all others. You can get that basic pattern almost anywhere. You can find it in mythology (the Greek Golden Age of Saturn, the Flood of Deucalion, and almost any number of figures - I like using Dionysus's death and resurrection at the hands of the Titans), occultism (Helena Blavatsky's Theosophism), or fiction (Robert E Howard's Conan and Kull stories). Hell, even Marvel Comics has it with Atlantis, the Cataclysm, and Varnae.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't do much to support this by including alternative interpretations. But there is some precedent. The Setites after all tell a different origin story. In my own chronicles, I routinely use older vampires relate the story in a different format. It's quite easy to do. And it doesn't need much imagination to do so.<br /> <br /> It just seems some people aren't able to read the text critically. But I immediately saw the potential for other interpretations when I first read the second edition corebook almost thirty years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T18:52:15-07:00","id":1390148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390140#post1390140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see a lot of posts on this forum like this, but I never had a problem like this. I don't think the game forces you to adopt Christianity or Abrahamic religion as objectively true. The fact that vampires ascribe their origins to a &quot;Caine&quot; is meaningless. While it makes total sense that Europeans in the Middle Ages would ascribe their origin to Cain, who was thought to be the father of many monsters, it would be absolutely ludicrous to think vampires from a pre-Christian tradition would ever think that to attribute their origins on the Holy Book of a small tribe of Jews. Especially those who were created before the Jewish people or the Kingdom of Israel ever existed. Obviously vampires in ancient Sumeria would NOT ascribe their origins to Cain. They would use another placeholder. And neither would the Classical Greeks or the early Romans.<br /> <br /> <b>Do you really think that Lucian, the NPC Gangrel vampire who marched with Julius Caesar, and was literally in the first edition of the corebook, was told by his sire that the origin of vampires lies in the text of the Jewish people, who were a recent and marginal acquisition of the Roman Empire during this lifetime?</b><br /> <br /> There are only a few essential elements that need to occur (and even this is debateable), and any other details are simply flavor text. You need an antedeluvian world. You need a Deluge. And you need someone to be the original vampire that spawned all others. You can get that basic pattern almost anywhere. You can find it in mythology (the Greek Golden Age of Saturn, the Flood of Deucalion, and almost any number of figures - I like using Dionysus's death and resurrection at the hands of the Titans), occultism (Helena Blavatsky's Theosophism), or fiction (Robert E Howard's Conan and Kull stories). Hell, even Marvel Comics has it with Atlantis, the Cataclysm, and Varnae.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't do much to support this by including alternative interpretations. But there is some precedent. The Setites after all tell a different origin story. In my own chronicles, I routinely use older vampires relate the story in a different format. It's quite easy to do. And it doesn't need much imagination to do so.<br /> <br /> It just seems some people aren't able to read the text critically. But I immediately saw the potential for other interpretations when I first read the second edition corebook almost thirty years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Caine is actually real then....yes?<br /> <br /> Though, in-universe, Caine isn't Jewish as he predates Abraham by 9000 years.<br /> <br /> In-universe, the Jewish people apparently got their legend of Adam and Eve and Caine from vampires. Not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Because, again, Goth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:29:41-07:00","id":1390168,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty obvious to me it\u2019s either a Christian-era rationalization of an older vampire myth, which may in turn have influenced the Judaic myth of Cain and Abel, or a Christian-era fabrication to begin with. There\u2019s just too much about the Noddist mythos that has nothing really to do with anything from the Bible or related texts, apart from a few names. Much easier to believe it\u2019s assimilation to Judaic tradition happened relatively recently (say, between one and two millennia ago). Interestingly, there\u2019s no trace of the Book of Nod before then, as the earliest manuscripts are medieval and most are even later. <br /> <br /> So either it\u2019s a Gnostic-style late reinterpretation of Biblical elements to suit a vampire audience or a Biblical-style reinterpretation of a prehistoric vampire myth of different origin, which doesn\u2019t survive in its earlier form. Either way it\u2019s interesting but far from solid evidence of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:31:30-07:00","id":1390190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390148#post1390148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Caine is actually real then....yes?<br /> <br /> Though, in-universe, Caine isn't Jewish as he predates Abraham by 9000 years.<br /> <br /> In-universe, the Jewish people apparently got their legend of Adam and Eve and Caine from vampires. Not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Because, again, Goth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, I'm not sure how you got that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine&quot; is simply a placeholder. It might be the Biblical Cain. It could be someone else in world mythology. It could be Varnae from Marvel Comics. Or Sauron from Numenor. Or someone else entirely.<br /> <br /> I think it is far more likely that Lucian's sire would have told him some story like &quot;You now possess a portion of the ichor of the gods, first seized by men during the Golden Age of Saturn. But when Jupiter overthrew Cronus, he cursed such men as he did Prometheus for stealing the secret of fire for Men. He attempted to destroy them in the Flood of Deucalion, but thirteen survived. The blood of one of those thirteen now resides in you.&quot; Or some other such variant. His sire might have used cultural elements from some other mythology he was more familiar with. Or he might have &quot;translated&quot; them into Greco-Roman myth in order to aid Lucian's comprehension.<br /> <br /> This is how I assume the current version of the vampire origin legend became associated with Cain and the Bible. In the long centuries of Christian and Muslim rule of mortals, these would have been the associations new vampires associated with concepts like a Flood, and their own association with Cain as a father of evil monsters, like how he was referred to in Beowulf. Since this is what was &quot;known&quot; when the sects of the Camarilla and Sabbat formed, this single version of the story became the official one.<br /> <br /> I'm sure someone like Critias who was embraced long before Christianity and would be familiar with many different pagan cultures, he heard many different variants of the same vampire myth - with various details changing, but a &quot;core&quot; group of facts remaining the same - there was once a single vampire from which all others were sprung; this was in the days before a Great Flood; only thirteen survived and all vampires are now descended from one of them.<br /> <br /> Assuming the Biblical stories are true in WoD, the Jews would have obtained their information on the antedeluvian world and the creation in the same way they obtained them in this world (if you believe in their religion) - oral tradition from Noah plus any divine revelation.<br /> <br /> Any stories told by vampires repeating what the clan founders told their childer would simply be in addition to that. Plus any other occult information revealed by any numerous ways about that world. You could have sleeping prophets like Edgar Cayce. Stories revealed by angels to the Celestial Chorus. Other remnants from the Deluge that survived. Lost artifacts and possibly even wraiths encountered in the Tempest or Stygia. Vampires aren't any more privileged in that regard. Except that the antedeluvians would have had first hand knowledge. But whatever they told their childer would not have been complete, probably misunderstood, and possibly deliberately misinformed.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the retention of (corrupted) lore as recorded by all the other world civilizations who simply didn't preserve such knowledge accurately.<br /> <br /> And if you want to go with some other culture's myth as more true, or your own version as the real thing, the same things hold true except the Jewish tradition also is corrupted to a degree and isn't as accurate as anyone else's stories.<br /> <br /> But even if you want the Biblical stories to be true, it does not mean that anyone outside of that tradition would be using terms found only in Jewish lore. Thousands of years since the Flood cause any such oral traditions to change, and by the time you get to Classical Greece, Rome, Persia, or India, many details are going to look different. It's like how the Indo-European peoples had one pantheon of gods with certain names, and 4000 years later you have a dozen or more different mythologies derived from it. The Norse, Celtic, and Greek religions all had the same source, yet they seem like they are totally different. The rate of change might be slower among vampires than humans, but it'll still happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-20-2020, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T02:50:49-07:00","id":1390235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390190#post1390190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, I'm not sure how you got that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine&quot; is simply a placeholder. It might be the Biblical Cain. It could be someone else in world mythology. It could be Varnae from Marvel Comics. Or Sauron from Numenor. Or someone else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that he might have just heard it from his sire or his sire's sire who heard it from their Antediluvian. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm just saying how obscure and unbelievable the story of Caine is, is up to the ST.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T04:12:26-07:00","id":1390248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> by advanced civilization I mean they had cities. I was just pointing out that not all non-Christian cultures in sub-Saharan Africa were \u201cprimitive.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wym \u201ctanned hollow?\u201d Idk what that means.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I think the Ashirra also accept the Caine narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T08:22:20-07:00","id":1390293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390248#post1390248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> by advanced civilization I mean they had cities. I was just pointing out that not all non-Christian cultures in sub-Saharan Africa were \u201cprimitive.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wym \u201ctanned hollow?\u201d Idk what that means.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I think the Ashirra also accept the Caine narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry tanned hollow is British slang for beaten badly or defeated utterly. Comes from how leather is beaten during treatment (or tanned)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-20-2020, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T09:40:27-07:00","id":1390308,"title":"","content":"Like what Black Fox is talking about, in my games I usually lean towards that before the rise of the Abrahamic religions, the use of the terms 'Caine' or 'Enoch' to describe The First and The First City were vanishing rare, if they existed at all they were likely limited to the Semitic peoples in there earliest proto forms.<br /> <br /> Vampires of the eldest generations recalled the stories of their elders from before The Flood and The Dark Father but a shroud of mystery cloaks that primordial age and so eventually by the time the grandchilder of The Antediluvian's grandchilder walked the night, the stories had split and transformed into a thousand regional variants.<br /> <br /> Now, after the rise of the Abrahamic Faiths and their successful claim to being the predominant cultural faith of the western world, the stories refer to Caine and Abel and Enoch. <br /> <br /> The part that I always come back to with thinking about it one way or another is this: do I prefer it being metacosmologically fluid in that The First Vampire is simply now referred to as Caine or if they have become Caine retrospectively due to consensus or if they, whether or not they always had been, as of now they were always Caine.<br /> <br /> Yeah, kind of a mind screw and not one I think I'll settle onto a personal answer for, both because the subject somewhat denies the pursuit of any one answer and also that I think either avenue can be used to the purpose of benefitting a story, either alone or together regardless of the seeming contradictions.<br /> <br /> Although what I ultimately tend to come down to is that Caine has probably accepted the title of Caine, but the name that Eve gave him when he was fresh from her womb has most likely been forever lost to the ravages of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T14:49:53-07:00","id":1390386,"title":"","content":"On a totally unrelated note, I just recently discovered that in San mythology, Cagn (an... adaptation of <b>\u01c0Kaggen) is the name of the God who created the universe and everything in it. Absolutely no relationship to Caine. Probably just a chance coincidence, but... one may wonder...</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T10:32:44-07:00","id":1390805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390308#post1390308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, after the rise of the Abrahamic Faiths and their successful claim to being the predominant cultural faith of the western world, the stories refer to Caine and Abel and Enoch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the Western world. Despite (or more likely, because of) the persecution of it, China is on pace to have more Christians than North America by 2030 and its already strong throughout Asia and Africa.<br /> <br /> Christians and Muslims account for over HALF of the world\u2019s population (est. 31.4% Christian, 23.2% Muslim per Pew Research study in 2015). Next highest is unaffiliated at 16.4% and then Hinduism at 15%, Buddism at 7.1%, Folk Religion at 5.9% and Other at 1%.<br /> <br /> Despite the Caine origin being controversial to the likely demographics of the player base, about 55% of the world\u2019s population (including the vast majority of Africa), at least by affiliation, professes belief in Adam, Eve, Cain, Abel and Enoch either literally or as an allegory.<br /> <br /> Thus, in a general population sense, Cain is about the least controversial choice it\u2019s possible to make for vampiric origins. His association with monsters was so understood that Grendel and his mother were described as the descendants of Cain in Beowulf (c. 1000 CE) without further explanation of why that lineage would make the monstrous, meaning it was already a common folk belief akin to how an American can say \u201cGeorge Washington and the cherry tree\u201d and not have to explain its meaning to a fellow American.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T10:44:39-07:00","id":1390810,"title":"","content":"Beowulf was written that late?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T11:53:02-07:00","id":1390819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390810#post1390810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beowulf was written that late?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somewhere between the 8th and 11th centuries, the surviving manuscript is from somewhere around 975-1025, the story and scholarship are really interesting and worth a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T11:59:16-07:00","id":1390822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390810#post1390810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beowulf was written that late?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it has Grendel as a descendant of Caine as said so it can't predate the Christianization of the Norse. Some people try and state it's an older tale modified but as a guy who got his Masters studying it, it's more like a Christian author's &quot;homage&quot; to Norse Mythology like an 10th century Tolkien.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-22-2020, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T12:08:14-07:00","id":1390825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390822#post1390822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it has Grendel as a descendant of Caine as said so it can't predate the Christianization of the Norse. Some people try and state it's an older tale modified but as a guy who got his Masters studying it, it's more like a Christian author's &quot;homage&quot; to Norse Mythology like an 10th century Tolkien.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you think it was originally an Anglo-Saxon story, or a Norse story? Really interested, and you are certainly more learned than me about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T12:19:42-07:00","id":1390828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388991-kindred-of-the-ebony-kingdom?p=1390825#post1390825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it was originally an Anglo-Saxon story, or a Norse story? Really interested, and you are certainly more learned than me about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think it was a Middle English Anglo-Saxon perspective on values and themes that were, even at the time, local folklore brought to the nation by the Viking invasions of the 7th century but preceding the Norman invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T12:40:24-07:00","id":1390830,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting is the actual description of Grendal... &quot;a creature of darkness, exiled from happiness and accursed of God, the destroyer and devourer of our human kind.\u201d<br /> <br /> While Grendel is traditionally depicted as a giant, that\u2019s not in the text... merely that Grendel was incredibly strong. He attacks only at night.<br /> <br /> Of further note.. Beowulf defeated Grendel without weapons by relying on his faith in God.<br /> <br /> Frankly, other than a specific association with blood drinking, the description of Grendel is basically in line with VtM... descendant of Cain, creature of darkness, exiled from happiness, accursed by God, feeds on humans, incredibly strong and is slain not by weapons, but by Beowulf\u2019s bare hands using true faith.<br /> <br /> And this was written down a millennium ago and, again, claims descent from Cain as the origin of his unholy power without further explanation... meaning common lore of the day was that Cain\u2019s descendants were monstrous.<br /> <br /> Which, for the topic at hand, is an argument that \u201cCain as father of monsters/vampires\u201d is something fairly widespread in Christian lands, which includes a good chunk of Africa for as long as there\u2019s been Christians. A Laibon would have to be nearly 2000 years old to have NOT heard of the Caine origin their entire life, by proximity to early Christian missionaries if nothing else.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s presuming the entire Caine-origin was completely made up from whole cloth vs. having at least some seed of truth behind it.<br /> <br /> And if only really ancient Methuselahs are old enough to remember some other story... does it really even matter how much of it is true or not?<br /> <br /> Or as I\u2019ve said... \u201csomeone had to be the first vampire. We may as well call him Caine.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 05-22-2020, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T12:51:55-07:00","id":1390832,"title":"","content":"My final opinion on it is the Laibon having the Caine myth works far far better than trying to assign the jianshi to Cainites if you're worried about cultural appropriation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:42:15-07:00","id":1390851,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:46:44-07:00","id":1390855,"title":"","content":"Glad we could help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon<